# Fixture: two identity lines, and the FIRST one declares a foreign version (audit #21, A.2.7
# review). The version it names is deliberately not the host's: that is what pins the ORDER of the
# refusals. Ask about the version first and this file is refused for being stale; while its identity
# is stated twice there is no line whose number can be trusted, so the duplicate is the first thing
# to say. The gate asserts both halves — that the refusal names the duplicate, and that it does not
# name the version.
plugin twin 1.0 api=1
plugin twin 1.0

panel twin "Twin" dock=bottom
  text "this panel must never be born"
